{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1143440-magic-for-mortals","id":1143440,"title":"Magic for mortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-09-24T06:52:56-07:00","id":1143440,"title":"Magic for mortals","content":"Hi all. I am a new Storyteller to WoD, having only played in a VtM game many years ago after playing Bloodlines (a common enough story, I'm sure). I want to run a game where my players are mortals and eventually develop into one of the different supernatural templates.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut my question is, if they want to take it slowly, how can I introduce magic into the game for them? Should I set them up as Proximi, or is there some kind of conversion for the 1e Second Sight splatbook? How do you guys handle this?<br /> <br /> \u200bThanks for any help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17639-ihrims\u00fb","name":"Ihrims\u00fb","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T07:11:09-07:00","id":1143443,"title":"","content":"The 2e conversion for Second Sight is really just the corebook supernatural merits. They're fluffed as psychic powers but if you want them to represent hedge magic you could just give them a coat of paint. <br /> <br /> Proximi? Sure. There's also wolf-blooded capable of rituals and the sorcerers from Dark Eras companion if you want to go nuts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T07:23:24-07:00","id":1143448,"title":"","content":"So... there are a lot of options, depending on how you want to interpret &quot;magic&quot; and where you want to take them.<br /> <br /> If you are going <b>Mage</b>, Proximi are a good intermediary phase. Alternatively, they could be Sleepwalkers with Relic Adept and a small collection of Artifacts. Or give them access to Rotes.<br /> <br /> <b>Promethean </b>has Alchemists.<br /> <br /> <b>Werewolf </b>has Wolf-blooded with the right Tell giving access to Pack Rites.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunter</b>, Witch Finders, added Witches, which are more scaled down. Those would need to be updated too, though.<br /> <br /> More generally, you could give them access to Supernatural Merits and treat those like magic abilities/spells (which they <i>are</i>). If you want a wizard-y feel, let them swap Supernatural Merits form a &quot;known&quot; list between Stories/Chapters. I've got a few ideas for items to improve things, if you want to go that route.<br /> <br /> Second Sight has been fan-updated a few times - search the forums and I'm sure you can find a few.<br /> <br /> Dark Eras, Beneath the Skin, has the super-Merit for Skin-Thieves. You might be able to mock up a magic system based entirely upon skinning ephemerals for their powers (or something based upon the mechanics without the skinning).<br /> <br /> Dark Eras Companion opens up Sorcery in the form of Open and Closed Rites. Basically, Do X, Y, and Z, and you get the magical effect. Open are ones anyone can use (like Abjuration), while Closed ones need a special Merit and learning more cost Integrity maximum.<br /> <br /> You could probably expand the basic Abjuration, Exorcism, Summoning, and Occult Skill stuff to do more &quot;magic-y&quot; stuff. Spirits and such could probably be bribed for magical action as well. All open to normal mortals, provided they know enough.<br /> <br /> Fan-stuff wise, there are Influence-based &quot;Mages&quot;, Changeling Contract-only Hedge Sorcerers, and Genii-as-Stigmatics (they make Gadgets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T07:27:05-07:00","id":1143451,"title":"","content":"And with the tells you can loosen up on which lets you do rites if you need to.<br /> <br /> I've always thought it was a bit silly that the one that helps with rites isn't one of the ones that lets you do them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T08:02:12-07:00","id":1143457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1143440-magic-for-mortals?p=1143451#post1143451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And with the tells you can loosen up on which lets you do rites if you need to.<br /> <br /> I've always thought it was a bit silly that the one that helps with rites isn't one of the ones that lets you do them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. But then, I let/houserule anyone with a Totem and a group do Pack Rites (it is the group activity combined with the Spirit/Totem that enables them; Wolf Rites require Essence, and are more tied to the Uratha's nature).<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Oh, and there are also the Micro-Templates in Hurt Locker, too. You could easily model magic using off of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T10:27:55-07:00","id":1143505,"title":"","content":"Also what a lot of people tend to forget is that any mortal can use the summoning, binding, warding and exorcising rules for ephemerals beings (spirits and ghosts). So a lot of supernaturel effects can be achieved via treating with a spirit or a ghost. There is also a lot of complications that can arise, but as a ST i tend to see that as a good thing.<br /> <br /> Edits: Youps, just noticed Vent0 mention exactly that options. Consider this post a +1 for that option then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":11312,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","user":"Maitrecorbo","date":". 09-24-2017, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T11:50:45-07:00","id":1143524,"title":"","content":"You might also look at Hurt Locker, which has a number of minor templates. A lot of them are more sci-fi flavored than what I tend to think of as 'magic' but that's a bit of semantic distinction, especially if you mean magic in the broader sense of supernatural powers as opposed to &quot;the thing that Mages do&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T13:23:03-07:00","id":1143561,"title":"","content":"I'd suggest Gutter Magic from Witch Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>SWTOR Referal: <a href=\"http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.swtor.com/r/JQ2nqy</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/414-gallus","name":"Gallus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"886"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-24T15:24:21-07:00","id":1143611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1143440-magic-for-mortals?p=1143451#post1143451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've always thought it was a bit silly that the one that helps with rites isn't one of the ones that lets you do them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, having ready access to accelerant isn't going to help you much personally if you have no means of starting a fire on your own timetable. Clever Fingers doesn't give you the sort of direct spiritual influence that the listed Tells provide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-25T06:22:56-07:00","id":1143756,"title":"","content":"For a mortal-to-supernatural game, I suggest starting by slowly introducing the mortal supernatural merits. Between core book, Hurt Locker, and manipulating ephemeral beings, you actually have a pretty good spread of abiilties for mortals to do a lot of things. Be wary of introducing the Hurt Locker micro-templates; those are pretty cool abilities, but they each have their own stories that might not mesh with your overall story idea, so could cause complications in the long run if you're not certain about them. <br /> <br /> As time goes on, and you decide what direction you want to take the game, think about transforming the mortals into half splats - ghouls, wolf-blood, sleepwalker, etc. Play that way for a bit as you slowly introduce the different supernatural societies. Then, once they're comfortable that way... bam. Full template. <br /> <br /> If the group is heavily invested in gonig different directions and interests, I recommend grabbign Beast the Primordial, since that does help a lot with crossover games. I also recommend staying away from Mage in terms of crossover - they add a lot of complexity to the game, and can often overshadow others easily, making the game unfun for many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}